---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/default-no-header.astro";
const title = "Optimizely CMS Marketing website redesign exploration ";
const bodyClass = "works";
import "../../styles/workspages.scss";
import Comparison from "../../layouts/components/comparison.astro";
---

<PageLayout title={title} bodyClass={bodyClass}>
	<main class="box workspage">
		<header class="inner section-header">
			<h1>
				Redesigning self-service widgets for product recommendations
			</h1>
			<article class="project-information">
				<div class="contributions">
					<h2>My Contributions</h2>
					<ul class="no-list">
						<li>UX/UI Design</li>
						<li>Design System</li>
						<li>Research & Testing</li>
						<li>Heuristic Evaluation</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<section class="details">
					<div class="challange">
						<h2>Challenge</h2>
						<p>
							The Optimizely CMS marketing website needed a
							redesign. I wanted to explore different visual
							directions and improve how the product's
							capabilities were presented.
						</p><p>
							Although my primary focus was product design, I took
							on this project as an opportunity to apply my skills
							to a marketing website and experiment with different
							approaches to visual storytelling and content
							presentation.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="team">
						<h2>Team</h2>
						<p>
							This was a personal design exploration, so I worked
							independently without a dedicated project team.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="discover">
						<h2>Approch</h2>
						<p>
							I followed a lightweight design process to explore
							possible improvements:
						</p>
						<ul class="no-list">
							<li>
								<b>Heuristic evaluation:</b> Reviewed the existing
								website to identify UX and visual design issues.
							</li>
							<li>
								<b>Competitor research:</b> Explored similar products,
								including Contentful and Adobe Experience Manager,
								using Gartner to understand industry patterns and
								design approaches.
							</li>
							<li>
								<b>Design exploration:</b> Developed four different
								page concepts based on my findings.
							</li>
							<li>
								<b>Peer review:</b> Planned to present the concepts
								to peers for feedback and refinement.
							</li>
							<li>
								<b>A/B testing:</b> Considered how the designs could
								be validated through A/B testing after implementation.
							</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="research">
						<h2>Research</h2>
						<p>
							I reviewed the existing website and documented my
							heuristic evaluation, including potential
							improvements, in a spreadsheet.
						</p>
						<p>
							For competitor research, I explored websites of key
							players in the CMS industry, including Contentful
							and Adobe Experience Manager. I captured screenshots
							and compared how they presented their products.
						</p>
						<p>Some interesting findings included:</p>
						<ul class="no-list">
							<li>
								Capabilities and benefits sections varied
								between long lists, columns, accordions, and
								tabs.
							</li>
							<li>
								Several websites used brand-colored text to
								highlight important information.
							</li>
							<li>
								Background choices varied, with most competitors
								using white, while others used black or blue.
							</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="solution">
						<h2>Solution</h2>
						<p>
							I developed four design directions, exploring
							different hero layouts, visual styles, and ways to
							present the Capabilities section using columns,
							tabs, accordions, and video.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="learning">
						<h2>Learning</h2>
						<p>
							This project helped me explore how visual design and
							content presentation can shape the way a product is
							communicated.
						</p>
					</div>
				</section>
			</article>
		</header>

		<section class="inner before-after">
			<h2>The Redesign</h2>
			<Comparison
				before="/images/works/opti-marketing-website/old-marketing-website.png"
				after="/images/works/opti-marketing-website/design3.png"
				beforeAlt="Previous design of optimizely marketing website"
				afterAlt="Proposed design 3"
			/>
		</section>

		<section class="inner">
			<article class="article">
				<figure>
					<img src="/images/works/opti-marketing-website/design1.png"
						alt="Design option 1"
					/>
					<figcaption>Design option 1</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-marketing-website/design2.png"
						alt="Design option 2"
					/>
					<figcaption>Design option 2</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure>
					<img
						src="/images/works/opti-marketing-website/design4.png"
						alt="Design option 4"
					/>
					<figcaption>Design option 4</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</article>
		</section>
	</main>
</PageLayout>
